\title{hsaCEtool: Habitat Selection Analysis Data Preparation for the Caribou Cumulative Effects Tool}
\description{
Steps for a 'targets' pipeline that prepares caribou location data and landscape layers for habitat selection analysis (integrated step selection analysis, iSSA) behind the caribou cumulative effects tool: reading and cleaning GPS locations, building tracks and random steps, building disturbance, fire, harvest, land cover, terrain and forest age layers (including a merged Yukon disturbance layer), extracting them along steps, and fitting the models. Settings are read from layered YAML files so one set of code serves many study areas.
